WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
- I heard Denzel called him

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.570
because y'all had worked together,

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.403
- Yeah.

00:00:04.403 --> 00:00:05.850
- And kinda was trying
to help you get the role

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:06.923
'cause he loved you and believed in you.

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:07.756
- Yeah.

00:00:07.756 --> 00:00:09.457
Do you think it's something
he said that was like,

00:00:09.457 --> 00:00:11.766
"No, I'm gonna see how
much he really will work?"

00:00:11.766 --> 00:00:13.221
- I don't know if that played into it,

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:14.054
it's possible.

00:00:14.054 --> 00:00:16.830
- I don't know that anyone
has that, in this business.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:21.030
Oh, Denzel called, and
like, Baz, and was like,

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.950
like, did he know Baz, like?

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.150
- [Austin] No they'd never met before.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:28.112
- And he just like, Denzel
Washington calls, right?

00:00:28.112 --> 00:00:29.160
- Yeah. I um, yeah.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.080
- Oh, no, look at your teary eyes.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.610
- Yeah, he's powerful.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.111
He's been my hero for so long

00:00:35.111 --> 00:00:37.650
and I went into that play going,

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.270
I'm not gonna try to be Denzel's friend.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:40.800
I'd read Ethan Hawke talking about them

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.000
doing Training Day together.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:42.833
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:43.680
- And he talked about this as well

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:44.880
and so I went in there and I thought,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.950
you know, I'm not, I'm
just gonna do my job,

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.260
and so I showed up the
first day of rehearsal,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.390
I memorized the four hour play,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.569
such an intense play, and we did it,

00:00:53.569 --> 00:00:55.920
and at a certain point,

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.599
Denzel started seeing that
I was showing up earlier

00:00:58.599 --> 00:01:00.570
than he was to get to the theater

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.250
so he'd show up a little bit earlier

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.050
and then I'd show up a little bit earlier,

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:04.883
- Challenge him.

00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:06.930
- Eventually one day it was just he and I,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.390
and he thought that he was
there before me and I came down,

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.220
I'd already been up in my dressing room,

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:13.410
and it is just the dark theater

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.450
and he's sitting on the stage by himself

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.507
and I came walking down and he goes,

00:01:16.507 --> 00:01:18.600
"Oh, I thought, I thought
I'd beat you here,"

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.464
and I said, "No, I've been
here for like an hour,"

00:01:20.464 --> 00:01:21.297
and he goes, you know,

00:01:21.297 --> 00:01:22.130
- but nice try.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.430
- "Come over, I got an idea for you,"

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:24.960
and he kind of took me under his wing

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:27.810
and started giving me
acting advice and, uh,

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.643
- Wow.

00:01:28.643 --> 00:01:30.270
- That was really huge for me,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.420
and then, he didn't tell me
he was gonna call Baz at all.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:34.860
He'd never met Baz.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.902
- That's so nice.

00:01:35.902 --> 00:01:36.735
- So very sweet.

00:01:36.735 --> 00:01:38.847
- I love that you, you made such an impact

00:01:38.847 --> 00:01:40.289
on him that he did something like that.

00:01:40.289 --> 00:01:41.122
- Very kind.

00:01:41.122 --> 00:01:42.423
- That's very, very cool.

